2026-08-10 10:04:44  round starting
Round 62 is complete and live at stamp 1786383743.

**What this round found and fixed** — August's second list was already worked in full, so the round took the carried faults, and each fix was verified by rendering:

1. **The "Nearest land" row finally fills.** Round 59's fill ran in `followShip` *above* the `passageCard()` call that creates the card, so on the only path a user can take the guard was always false and every slip showed the placeholder. The fill now lives in `passageCard()` itself — the function that writes the row writes its value — with honest null returns: a dash means the router isn't ready, "none within 486 nm" means the scan ran and found nothing. Verified on screen: "Cobh · 55 nm N" off the Great Western, "Tazerka Oil Terminal · 32 nm WSW" off the carrier in the Strait of Sicily.

2. **The wrong-era voyage hash no longer hangs the app.** `#e=3&f=zhenghe` held `__FRAME_READY` through 900 retries hunting a 1415 voyage in an AD 500–1400 fleet. A voyage now names its own era from its year, outranking a contradictory `e=`; two more gate leaks closed alongside (unknown ids, and a give-up branch that never released the gate it held). The diagnosis frame for this fix also caught **"12° 60′ N"** on the position readout — degrees and minutes rounded separately — now rounded once, in minutes.

3. **The label-flap false RED struck a ninth time, and reading the diff as an image overturned its story.** It was never font ghosting this time — the labels were *absent*, with one sea name frozen where a mid-boot camera had projected it. `markReady()` never asked whether the label layer had caught up with the camera; it now requires a settled label pass before a frozen capture can fire.

Also recovered: rounds 59–61 shipped without handoffs (the recurring omission) — reconstructed in HANDOFF.md from commit bodies and FRAME-LOG. The loop prompt's stale "25 hulls" is corrected to the real rule.

**Closing state:** audit 29/29 twice, ratchet 41/41 green with the four moved aboard frames classified (land-row text wrap reflowing the card, scene untouched) and accepted with reasons, globe-default 0.000% on the final run, both commits pushed, live stamp verified. Next round: the shipwright detail gaps continue — furled sails, anchors, wooldings, the waterway.
