## Round 98 summary

The queue stands worked in full (r57), so this round took round 97's named leftover: **Azzam's stern terraces**, the last big silhouette gap between the model and the broadside.

**The measurement came first, and it corrected round 97's read.** A 0.0025-u envelope scan of the Fricke broadside resolved the main-deck bulwark ending at u 0.884 — the 9.93 m reading at exactly 0.900 is an occluder standing on the terrace — and showed every terrace cap **raking** down toward its own break: 9.9→9.6 m, then 6.9→7.0, 6.6→6.1, 5.7→4.9, 4.9→4.2, and 3.5→3.0 m at the transom. That went into a new `sternSteps` record: measured cap lines per span, derived decks behind them (the plate cannot see decks behind their own bulwarks, and the provenance says so).

**The build is hull-sheer surgery, record-gated end to end.** `sheer()` steps the deck line span by span; `hullStations()` inserts 4 mm snap-pair stations at every break — the snapBand lesson in its third guise, a height on a vertex cannot have an edge — and shell, deck and frames follow because they all ask `surfacePoint`. New `buildSternTerraces()` closes each break with a cambered riser, walks solid parapets flush with the shell (counter flare included), rides a dark cap along every top, and walls the transom. The old deck-edge rail is suppressed there — the bulwark owns that edge now.

